      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "INTRODUCTION",
          "content": "We report a case of transomental herniation of the ileum through a defect in the gastrocolic ligament with re-emergence through a defect in the gastrohepatic ligament. This type of herniation is extremely rare and a review of the literature is presented."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CLINICAL PRESENTATION",
          "content": "A 41-year-old Chinese male presented with signs and symptoms of intestinal obstruction."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "TREATMENT",
          "content": "An urgent laparotomy was undertaken and he was found to have a rare form of intra-abdominal hernia. The hernia was reduced and the defects were closed."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "OUTCOME",
          "content": "Postoperative recovery was unremarkable."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Urgent operation should not be delayed because of the high mortality associated with strangulation."
        }
      ]},
